				"uid" : {
					"__type" : "uid",
					"uidString" : "WyCdt5QNTEiE/2TV3uFf1A=="
				},
				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "You made it through the second part, too! Before you go, a bit of honesty: gt4carp is usable, but it is far from finished. The biggest gap is distribution. The server is a binary built with Metacarp, and there is no nice way to ship it with the GT package yet."
			},
			{
				"__type" : "textSnippet",
				"children" : {
					"__type" : "snippets",
					"items" : [ ]
				},
				"createEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"createTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-09-26T21:49:16.267433+02:00"
					}
				},
				"editEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"editTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-09-26T21:49:16.267433+02:00"
					}
				},
				"uid" : {
					"__type" : "uid",
					"uidString" : "u6TlQH/NQO+Z8f7XF6sbug=="
				},
				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "Cells don’t have identities either. The server sees source that defines `foo`, then source that defines `bar`, and can’t tell a new snippet from a renamed one, so old definitions can linger as ghosts. Reopening a module from a second snippet replaces what the first one defined. `DECISIONS.md` lays out the options, but I haven’t picked one yet."
			},
			{
				"__type" : "textSnippet",
				"children" : {
					"__type" : "snippets",
					"items" : [ ]
				},
				"createEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"createTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-09-26T21:49:16.267433+02:00"
					}
				},
				"editEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"editTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-09-26T21:49:16.267433+02:00"
					}
				},
				"uid" : {
					"__type" : "uid",
					"uidString" : "DG5bQqYYRkqoyyYpJnYCLw=="
				},
				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "And warm state can degrade quietly. The server falls back to slower paths to stay correct, but GT doesn’t tell you when it does, so things just get slower, and you are left wondering why."
			},
			{
				"__type" : "textSnippet",
				"children" : {
					"__type" : "snippets",
					"items" : [ ]
				},
				"createEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
